within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.N_NervousSystem.N02B_OtherAnalgesicsAndAntipyretics.N02BF01_Gabapentin;
model Gabapentin_Zhou2026_PD_vas
  "emax exposure-response sweep — Zhou_2026 :: VAS (pain intensity)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 7.31,      // [1]
    Emax = -1,  // [1]
    EC50 = 0.00026311,  // [kg/m3; ng/mL × 1e-06]
    gamma = 1,
    exposure_per_s = 1e-06);   // 1 ng/mL per second
  // imax_as_negative_emax: Imax (Q323) enters SigmoidEmaxSweep as −Emax
  // defaulted: gamma
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 2700, Interval = 5.4),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Gabapentin_Zhou2026_PD_vas</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Zhou L et al., <i>Frontiers in pharmacology 17:1760901</i> 2026 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3389/fphar.2026.1760901\">doi:10.3389/fphar.2026.1760901</a>) — pain intensity against gabapentin ng/mL — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =       7.31          drug-free response (baseline) (E0, Q324)
  Emax  =          1          maximal effect term (Imax, Q323)
  EC50  =     263.11 ng/mL    exposure at half of the maximal effect term (IC50, Q322)
  gamma = (library default) Hill coefficient</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one ng/mL of gabapentin per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 7.31   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (263.11 ng/mL)  response 6.81
  exposure -> infinity  response 6.31</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Zhou_2026: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Gabapentin_Zhou2026_PD_vas;
